,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469445474,"data":"  It does NOT test behaviour in a genuinely full cabin. The dataset never\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469450402,"data":"  exceeds 4 occupants and this subset tops out lower, so the crowded regime\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469455041,"data":"  that the product exists to measure is entirely unobserved.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469460315,"data":"  Ground truth is model-generated pseudo-labels, not human annotation.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469465237,"data":"  Single 32-minute daytime session: nothing here speaks to low light.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469470274,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469475353,"data":"  Statistical fragility:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.46948018,"data":"   - sparse levels (fewer than 100 frames): count 3: n=59\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469484882,"data":"   - highest occupancy observed is 3; the dataset never exceeds 4 and this subset tops out lower still, so nothing here speaks to a full cabin\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469490118,"data":"  Correlation point estimates above are reported with bootstrap intervals\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.469495239,"data":"  precisely because the point estimate alone would look more solid than it is.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":334.470317901,"data":"\n"}
